FeatherTail for Debian / Proxmox VE
===================================

FeatherTail is a Proxmox host agent for FeatherPanel. It Depends on
`pve-manager`, so apt will only install it on Proxmox VE nodes that already
have the Proxmox repositories configured.

It runs as a systemd service, manages DHCP leases by VMID, installs bundled
noVNC assets, and exposes an HTTP API for the panel.

Quick start
-----------

1. Edit the configuration:

       sudo nano /etc/feathertail/feathertail.toml

   Set a strong `api_token` and your DHCP network settings before exposing the API.

2. Enable and start the service (done automatically on Proxmox hosts):

       sudo systemctl enable --now feathertail

3. Check status:

       systemctl status feathertail
       journalctl -u feathertail -f

Configuration lives in `/etc/feathertail/feathertail.toml`. The binary is
installed to `/usr/local/bin/feathertail`. Lease data defaults to
`/var/lib/feathertail/dhcp.sqlite3`.

Channels
--------

- `feathertail` — stable releases (GitHub `v*` tags)
- `feathertail-dev` — per-commit builds from `main`

These packages conflict with each other and cannot be installed together.
Switch channels with apt (the other package is replaced automatically).

Upgrades
--------

Existing configuration is preserved on upgrade (`config|noreplace`):

       sudo apt-get install --only-upgrade feathertail
       # or
       sudo apt-get install --only-upgrade feathertail-dev

